---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
import Seg from '../../../components/sim/Seg.astro';
import Result from '../../../components/sim/Result.astro';
import Caption from '../../../components/sim/Caption.astro';
import Readout from '../../../components/sim/Readout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="deep-learning"
  title="Embeddings & Cosine Similarity"
  description="An embedding turns a word into an arrow, and two words are similar when their arrows point the same way. Rank the same words by distance instead and the answers change."
  shortcuts={['fullscreen']}
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-view">
      <div class="sim-stage">
        <canvas
          id="cos"
          width="1000"
          height="600"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Word vectors as arrows from a common origin, a draggable query arrow, and the angle or distance between the query and the word it is compared with."
        ></canvas>
      </div>
      <Caption
        legend={[
          { label: 'the query', color: '#7c8cff' },
          { label: 'the word compared with it', color: '#5eead4' },
          { label: 'the rest of the vocabulary', color: 'rgba(160,165,175,0.6)' },
        ]}
        hint="Drag anywhere to move the query · click a word to compare with it"
      />
      <Result label="Similarity with its best match" />
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <Seg id="score" label="Rank the words by" attr="s" options={[{ value: 'cos', label: 'cos θ' }, { value: 'dot', label: 'dot product' }, { value: 'euc', label: 'distance' }]} />
      <div class="control">
        <label for="compare">Compare the query with</label>
        <select id="compare">
          <option value="best">its best match</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="wlist" id="list"></div>
      <div class="control">
        <div class="checks">
          <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="unit" /> <span>Force the query to length 1</span></label>
          <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="proj" checked /> <span id="projlbl">Show the shadow the query casts</span></label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Readout
        title="Values"
        rows={[
          { id: 'r-ang', label: 'angle θ' },
          { id: 'r-cos', label: 'cos θ' },
          { id: 'r-dot', label: 'dot product' },
          { id: 'r-euc', label: 'distance ‖q − w‖' },
          { id: 'r-qlen', label: 'query length' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Swing the query around the circle. The match changes the moment the
      <b>angle</b> changes, and it never changes while you only make the arrow
      longer or shorter. Cosine similarity divides the length out, so it measures
      <b>direction alone</b>.
    </li>
    <li>
      cos θ runs from <b>1</b> (same direction, same meaning) through <b>0</b> (at
      right angles, unrelated) to <b>−1</b> (opposite). Lay the query straight on
      <b>puppy</b> and the number reads 1.00, with dog just behind it, car near 0
      and king below zero. Those numbers are the whole of semantic search.
    </li>
    <li>
      Turn on the shadow. The dashed line drops the query tip onto the word's
      direction, and the bright segment left behind has length |q| cos θ. That
      shadow is what the dot product measures; the cosine is the same shadow after
      dividing by both lengths.
    </li>
    <li>
      Now switch the ranking to <b>dot product</b>. The generic word <b>thing</b>,
      drawn long because it appears everywhere, takes over the top spot from
      whatever you are actually pointing at. Raw dot products reward long vectors,
      which is exactly why retrieval systems normalise and use the cosine.
    </li>
    <li>
      Tick <b>force the query to length 1</b>. Every arrow now sits on the circle,
      the dot product and the cosine become the same number, and the shadow is
      literally cos θ. Normalised embeddings are used precisely so these two agree.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch the ranking to <b>distance</b>. The picture changes shape: the
      cosine's level sets are <b>rays out of the origin</b>, so length is
      invisible to it, while distance measures rings <b>around the query tip</b>,
      so a word can lose simply by being long. Watch <b>kitten</b>, a short arrow,
      beat <b>cat</b> whenever your query is short, even though cat points more
      the way you are pointing.
    </li>
    <li>
      Then put both on the circle: tick <b>length 1</b> and click a word whose
      arrow is already about that long. Now the two rankings agree, always, and
      they must, because ‖q−w‖² = 2 − 2 cos θ when both have length one. That one
      identity is why a vector database can index cosine similarity with a
      nearest-neighbour structure that only knows how to measure distance.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText } from '../../../lib/sim';
  import { equation } from '../../../lib/equation';
  import { stageInk } from '../../../lib/draw';
  import { el, segmented, check, result, readout } from '../../../lib/panel';

  const ACCENT = '#7c8cff', TEAL = '#5eead4';
  const canvas = el('cos') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const { ink } = stageInk(canvas);
  const { label } = makeText(ctx, ink);
  const setEq = equation();
  const setResult = result();
  const setRows = readout();

  // A hand-made two-dimensional "embedding": words that mean similar things
  // point the same way, and `thing` is long the way a very frequent generic
  // word is long in a real model.
  const WORDS = [
    { w: 'king', a: 76, r: 0.84 }, { w: 'queen', a: 102, r: 0.79 }, { w: 'cat', a: 162, r: 0.92 },
    { w: 'kitten', a: 180, r: 0.58 }, { w: 'dog', a: 204, r: 0.96 }, { w: 'puppy', a: 224, r: 0.62 },
    { w: 'thing', a: 244, r: 1.42 }, { w: 'car', a: 316, r: 0.88 }, { w: 'truck', a: 334, r: 0.74 },
  ];
  const state = { qa: (232 * Math.PI) / 180, ql: 0.8, score: 'cos' as 'cos' | 'dot' | 'euc', compare: 'best', unit: false, proj: true };

  const C = { x: W / 2, y: H / 2, R: 185 };
  const rad = (deg: number) => (deg * Math.PI) / 180;
  const toX = (a: number, r: number) => C.x + C.R * r * Math.cos(a);
  const toY = (a: number, r: number) => C.y - C.R * r * Math.sin(a);
  const qlen = () => (state.unit ? 1 : state.ql);
  const cosOf = (a: number) => Math.cos(a - state.qa);
  const dotOf = (a: number, r: number) => qlen() * r * Math.cos(a - state.qa);
  const eucOf = (a: number, r: number) => Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, qlen() ** 2 + r * r - 2 * qlen() * r * Math.cos(a - state.qa)));
  const scoreOf = (word: { a: number; r: number }) =>
    state.score === 'cos' ? cosOf(rad(word.a)) : state.score === 'dot' ? dotOf(rad(word.a), word.r) : -eucOf(rad(word.a), word.r);
  const shownOf = (word: { a: number; r: number }) => (state.score === 'euc' ? eucOf(rad(word.a), word.r) : scoreOf(word));
  const ranked = () => WORDS.map((x) => ({ ...x, s: scoreOf(x) })).sort((p, q) => q.s - p.s);
  function target() {
    if (state.compare !== 'best') {
      const f = WORDS.find((x) => x.w === state.compare);
      if (f) return f;
    }
    return ranked()[0];
  }

  function arrow(a: number, r: number, colour: string, width: number) {
    const x = toX(a, r), y = toY(a, r);
    ctx.strokeStyle = colour;
    ctx.lineWidth = width;
    ctx.lineCap = 'round';
    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(C.x, C.y); ctx.lineTo(x, y); ctx.stroke();
    const head = 5 + width * 1.8;
    ctx.fillStyle = colour;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x - head * Math.cos(a - 0.38), y + head * Math.sin(a - 0.38));
    ctx.lineTo(x - head * Math.cos(a + 0.38), y + head * Math.sin(a + 0.38));
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fill();
  }

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    const t = target();
    const ta = rad(t.a), q = state.qa;
    const c = cosOf(ta);
    const theta = (Math.acos(Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, c))) * 180) / Math.PI;
    const dist = eucOf(ta, t.r);
    const euc = state.score === 'euc';

    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.16);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.setLineDash([3, 5]);
    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(C.x, C.y, C.R, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    label('length 1', C.x + C.R + 8, C.y - 6, 0.3, 'left', 11.5);

    if (state.proj && !euc) {
      const shadow = qlen() * c;
      ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.14);
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(toX(ta, -1.5), toY(ta, -1.5)); ctx.lineTo(toX(ta, 1.7), toY(ta, 1.7)); ctx.stroke();
      ctx.strokeStyle = TEAL;
      ctx.lineWidth = 6;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.35;
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(C.x, C.y); ctx.lineTo(toX(ta, shadow), toY(ta, shadow)); ctx.stroke();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.35);
      ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(toX(q, qlen()), toY(q, qlen())); ctx.lineTo(toX(ta, shadow), toY(ta, shadow)); ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      label(`shadow ${shadow.toFixed(2)}`, toX(ta, shadow / 2) + 10, toY(ta, shadow / 2) + 14, 1, 'left', 11.5, TEAL);
    }
    if (euc) {
      const qxp = toX(q, qlen()), qyp = toY(q, qlen());
      if (state.proj) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.12);
        ctx.setLineDash([2, 5]);
        ctx.lineWidth = 1;
        for (const rr of [0.35, 0.7, 1.05, 1.4]) { ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(qxp, qyp, C.R * rr, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.stroke(); }
        ctx.setLineDash([]);
      }
      ctx.strokeStyle = `${TEAL}66`;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(qxp, qyp, C.R * dist, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.stroke();
      ctx.strokeStyle = TEAL;
      ctx.lineWidth = 3;
      ctx.setLineDash([6, 4]);
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(qxp, qyp); ctx.lineTo(toX(ta, t.r), toY(ta, t.r)); ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      label(dist.toFixed(2), (qxp + toX(ta, t.r)) / 2, (qyp + toY(ta, t.r)) / 2 - 8, 1, 'center', 11.5, TEAL);
    }
    // the angle between them
    let a0 = q, a1 = ta;
    if (((a1 - a0 + Math.PI * 4) % (Math.PI * 2)) > Math.PI) [a0, a1] = [a1, a0];
    if (!euc) {
      ctx.fillStyle = `${TEAL}22`;
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(C.x, C.y); ctx.arc(C.x, C.y, 74, -a0, -a1, true); ctx.closePath(); ctx.fill();
      const mid = (a0 + a1) / 2 + (((a1 - a0 + Math.PI * 4) % (Math.PI * 2)) > Math.PI ? Math.PI : 0);
      label(`${theta.toFixed(0)}°`, C.x + 92 * Math.cos(mid), C.y - 92 * Math.sin(mid) + 4, 0.7, 'center', 11);
    }
    for (const word of WORDS) {
      const a = rad(word.a);
      const on = word.w === t.w;
      arrow(a, word.r, on ? TEAL : ink(0.3), on ? 3 : 1.6);
      label(word.w, toX(a, word.r) + 14 * Math.cos(a), toY(a, word.r) - 14 * Math.sin(a) + 4, on ? 1 : 0.5, Math.cos(a) < -0.25 ? 'right' : Math.cos(a) > 0.25 ? 'left' : 'center', on ? 13 : 12, on ? TEAL : undefined);
    }
    arrow(q, qlen(), ACCENT, 3.4);
    ctx.fillStyle = ACCENT;
    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(toX(q, qlen()), toY(q, qlen()), 7, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
    label('query', toX(q, qlen()) + 26 * Math.cos(q), toY(q, qlen()) - 26 * Math.sin(q) + 4, 1, Math.cos(q) < -0.25 ? 'right' : Math.cos(q) > 0.25 ? 'left' : 'center', 12, ACCENT);

    words(c, theta, dist, t);
  }

  const listEl = el('list');
  function words(c: number, theta: number, dist: number, t: { w: string; r: number }) {
    const rows = ranked();
    const euc = state.score === 'euc';
    const span = Math.max(...rows.map((r) => Math.abs(r.s)), 0.001);
    listEl.innerHTML = rows
      .map((r) => {
        const shown = shownOf(r);
        const w = euc ? (1 - Math.abs(r.s) / span) * 100 : (Math.abs(r.s) / span) * 50;
        const side = euc ? 'left:0' : r.s >= 0 ? 'left:50%' : 'right:50%';
        return `<div class="cs-row${euc ? ' full' : ''}${r.w === t.w ? ' sel' : ''}" data-w="${r.w}"><span class="nm">${r.w}</span><span class="bar"><i style="${side};width:${w}%"></i><s></s></span><b>${shown.toFixed(2)}</b></div>`;
      })
      .join('');
    el('projlbl').textContent = euc ? 'Show rings of equal distance' : 'Show the shadow the query casts';

    const dot = qlen() * t.r * c;
    const Q = (x: string) => `\\textcolor{${ACCENT}}{${x}}`, Wc = (x: string) => `\\textcolor{${TEAL}}{${x}}`;
    setEq({
      rule: euc
        ? [`\\lVert ${Q('q')} - ${Wc('w')} \\rVert^2 = \\lVert q\\rVert^2 + \\lVert w\\rVert^2 - 2\\,q\\cdot w`]
        : [`\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{${Q('q')}\\cdot ${Wc('w')}}{\\lVert q\\rVert\\,\\lVert w\\rVert}`, '\\qquad', `q\\cdot w = \\lVert q\\rVert\\,\\lVert w\\rVert\\cos\\theta`],
      live: euc
        ? [[`\\lVert q - w\\rVert = ${dist.toFixed(3)}`, TEAL], `\\quad\\theta = ${theta.toFixed(1)}^\\circ`, `\\quad\\lVert q\\rVert = ${qlen().toFixed(2)},\\ \\lVert w\\rVert = ${t.r.toFixed(2)}`]
        : [[`\\cos\\theta = ${c.toFixed(3)}`, TEAL], `\\quad\\theta = ${theta.toFixed(1)}^\\circ`, `\\quad q\\cdot w = ${dot.toFixed(3)}`],
    });
    const best = state.compare === 'best';
    el('result-label').textContent = euc ? `Distance to ${best ? 'its nearest word' : t.w}` : `Similarity with ${best ? 'its best match' : t.w}`;
    setResult({
      value: euc ? dist.toFixed(2) : c.toFixed(2),
      colour: TEAL,
      status: `${t.w} · θ = ${theta.toFixed(1)}° · q·w = ${dot.toFixed(2)} · ‖q − w‖ = ${dist.toFixed(2)}`,
      note: euc
        ? Math.abs(qlen() - t.r) < 0.06
          ? 'Both arrows are about the same length, so this distance is just 2 − 2 cos θ: distance and cosine agree.'
          : 'Distance measures rings around the query tip, so a word can lose by being long even when it points the right way.'
        : state.score === 'dot'
          ? 'The dot product is the shadow times the query length, so long vectors like thing win regardless of direction.'
          : 'Cosine divides the lengths out and keeps only the angle: making either arrow longer changes nothing.',
    });
    setRows({ 'r-ang': `${theta.toFixed(1)}°`, 'r-cos': c.toFixed(3), 'r-dot': dot.toFixed(3), 'r-euc': dist.toFixed(3), 'r-qlen': qlen().toFixed(2) });
  }

  const sel = el('compare') as HTMLSelectElement;
  for (const word of WORDS) {
    const o = document.createElement('option');
    o.value = word.w;
    o.textContent = word.w;
    sel.appendChild(o);
  }
  sel.addEventListener('change', () => { state.compare = sel.value; draw(); });
  listEl.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const row = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('.cs-row') as HTMLElement | null;
    if (!row) return;
    state.compare = state.compare === row.dataset.w ? 'best' : row.dataset.w!;
    sel.value = state.compare;
    draw();
  });
  segmented('score', (s) => { state.score = s as 'cos' | 'dot' | 'euc'; draw(); });
  check('unit', (on) => { state.unit = on; draw(); });
  check('proj', (on) => { state.proj = on; draw(); });

  let dragging = false;
  const pointer = (e: PointerEvent) => {
    const b = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
    return { x: ((e.clientX - b.left) / b.width) * W, y: ((e.clientY - b.top) / b.height) * H };
  };
  function setQuery(p: { x: number; y: number }) {
    const dx = p.x - C.x, dy = C.y - p.y;
    state.qa = Math.atan2(dy, dx);
    if (!state.unit) state.ql = Math.max(0.15, Math.min(1.5, Math.hypot(dx, dy) / C.R));
    draw();
  }
  canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
    const p = pointer(e);
    for (const word of WORDS) {
      const a = rad(word.a);
      if (Math.hypot(p.x - toX(a, word.r), p.y - toY(a, word.r)) < 22) {
        state.compare = state.compare === word.w ? 'best' : word.w;
        sel.value = state.compare;
        draw();
        return;
      }
    }
    dragging = true;
    canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
    setQuery(p);
  });
  canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (dragging) setQuery(pointer(e)); });
  canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', () => (dragging = false));
  canvas.addEventListener('pointercancel', () => (dragging = false));

  draw();
</script>

<style>
  #cos {
    cursor: crosshair;
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .sim-panel select {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 7px 9px;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .wlist {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
  }
</style>

<!-- The ranking rows are injected via innerHTML, so they never carry Astro's
     scoped attribute; these rules have to be global to reach them. -->
<style is:global>
  .cs-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 58px 1fr 40px;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    padding: 4px 5px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .cs-row:hover {
    background: var(--bg-elev);
  }
  .cs-row.sel {
    background: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .cs-row .nm {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .cs-row.sel .nm {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .cs-row .bar {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    height: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .cs-row .bar i {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    background: var(--accent);
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
  .cs-row.sel .bar i {
    background: var(--accent-2);
    opacity: 0.9;
  }
  .cs-row.full .bar s {
    display: none;
  }
  .cs-row .bar s {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--border-strong);
  }
  .cs-row b {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-align: right;
    color: var(--accent-2);
  }
</style>
